<section class="tm-s tm-cv" id="convert"><div class="tm-w"><div class="tm-sh"><p class="tm-ey"><svg class="tm-rt" viewBox="0 0 60 30" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 18c6-10 18-12 26-8s18 2 24-4c2 6-2 14-12 16s-16 0-22 2S6 26 4 18z"/><path d="M20 12c-2-4 0-8 4-10M38 12c2-4 6-6 10-6" /></svg> Tool one</p><h2 class="rv">Turmeric converter</h2><p class="tm-p">A recipe calls for fresh root and you only have powder, or the other way round? As a rule of thumb, 1 inch of fresh root gives about 1 tablespoon grated, which equals about 1 teaspoon ground.</p></div>
<div class="tm-cv-g"><div class="tm-cv-c"><div class="tm-seg" id="cv-u" role="group" aria-label="I have"><button type="button" data-v="0" class="on">Fresh root (inches)</button><button type="button" data-v="1">Grated (tbsp)</button><button type="button" data-v="2">Ground (tsp)</button></div>
<label class="tm-lb" for="cv-a">Amount <output id="cv-ao">2</output></label><input type="range" id="cv-a" min=".5" max="6" step=".5" value="2"><figure class="tm-cv-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1768729340925-2749ecdc211c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=600&h=260&q=75" alt="turmeric root, dried pieces and powder on a wooden board" width="600" height="260" loading="lazy"></figure></div>
<div class="tm-jars" aria-live="polite"><div class="tm-jar"><div class="tm-jar-g"><i id="cv-j0"></i></div><b id="cv-r0">2 in</b><span>Fresh root</span></div><div class="tm-jar"><div class="tm-jar-g"><i id="cv-j1"></i></div><b id="cv-r1">2 tbsp</b><span>Freshly grated</span></div><div class="tm-jar"><div class="tm-jar-g"><i id="cv-j2"></i></div><b id="cv-r2">2 tsp</b><span>Ground powder</span></div><p class="tm-small" id="cv-n"></p></div></div></div></section>

<section class="tm-s tm-tk" id="tadka"><div class="tm-w tm-tk-g"><div class="tm-pan-w"><div class="tm-pan"><div class="tm-oil" id="tk-oil"></div><div class="tm-seeds" id="tk-seeds" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><div class="tm-handle" aria-hidden="true"></div><p class="tm-clock"><b id="tk-t">0:00</b><span id="tk-s">Ready when you are</span></p></div>
<div><p class="tm-ey"><svg class="tm-rt" viewBox="0 0 60 30" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 18c6-10 18-12 26-8s18 2 24-4c2 6-2 14-12 16s-16 0-22 2S6 26 4 18z"/><path d="M20 12c-2-4 0-8 4-10M38 12c2-4 6-6 10-6" /></svg> Tool two</p><h2 class="rv">Tadka timer</h2><p class="tm-p">A tadka, or tempering, is spices bloomed in hot oil or ghee and poured over a dish at the end. Order and timing matter: turmeric goes in last and only for seconds, so it never burns. Pick a dish and follow along.</p>
<div class="tm-seg" id="tk-d" role="group" aria-label="Dish"><button type="button" data-v="0" class="on">Dal</button><button type="button" data-v="1">Vegetable curry</button><button type="button" data-v="2">Lemon rice</button></div>
<ol class="tm-steps" id="tk-l"></ol><div class="tm-tk-b"><button type="button" class="tm-btn" id="tk-go">Start the tadka</button><button type="button" class="tm-ghost" id="tk-r">Reset</button></div><figure class="tm-tk-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1708782344490-9026aaa5eec7?auto=format&fit=crop&w=600&h=260&q=75" alt="a bowl of curry beside a bowl of rice" width="600" height="260" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="tm-s tm-bx"><div class="tm-w tm-bx-g"><div><p class="tm-ey"><svg class="tm-rt" viewBox="0 0 60 30" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 18c6-10 18-12 26-8s18 2 24-4c2 6-2 14-12 16s-16 0-22 2S6 26 4 18z"/><path d="M20 12c-2-4 0-8 4-10M38 12c2-4 6-6 10-6" /></svg> The spice box</p><h2 class="rv">Turmeric and its neighbours</h2><p class="tm-p">Most Indian kitchens keep a round steel spice box, the masala dabba, with seven everyday spices. Turmeric sits in the middle. Tap a cup to meet each one.</p><div class="tm-sp" aria-live="polite"><b id="sp-n">Turmeric</b><em id="sp-h">Haldi</em><p id="sp-d"></p></div><figure class="tm-bx-i rv rv-c"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1784382265443-b90fc6b9c349?auto=format&fit=crop&w=600&h=260&q=75" alt="colourful ground spices in gold-rimmed bowls" width="600" height="260" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div class="tm-dabba"><div class="tm-dabba-r"><button type="button" class="tm-cup on" data-i="0" style="left:50.0%;top:50.0%;--c:#E3A018" aria-label="Turmeric"><i></i></button><button type="button" class="tm-cup" data-i="1" style="left:50.0%;top:19.3%;--c:#8A5A2B" aria-label="Cumin"><i></i></button><button type="button" class="tm-cup" data-i="2" style="left:76.6%;top:34.7%;--c:#3B2A22" aria-label="Mustard seed"><i></i></button><button type="button" class="tm-cup" data-i="3" style="left:76.6%;top:65.3%;--c:#B89A5A" aria-label="Coriander"><i></i></button><button type="button" class="tm-cup" data-i="4" style="left:50.0%;top:80.7%;--c:#B3261E" aria-label="Chilli"><i></i></button><button type="button" class="tm-cup" data-i="5" style="left:23.4%;top:65.3%;--c:#C9923A" aria-label="Fenugreek"><i></i></button><button type="button" class="tm-cup" data-i="6" style="left:23.4%;top:34.7%;--c:#6E8B3D" aria-label="Cardamom"><i></i></button></div></div></div></section>

<section class="tm-s tm-fl"><div class="tm-w"><div class="tm-sh tm-sh-c"><p class="tm-ey"><svg class="tm-rt" viewBox="0 0 60 30" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 18c6-10 18-12 26-8s18 2 24-4c2 6-2 14-12 16s-16 0-22 2S6 26 4 18z"/><path d="M20 12c-2-4 0-8 4-10M38 12c2-4 6-6 10-6" /></svg> From root to powder</p><h2 class="rv">How turmeric reaches your kitchen</h2></div><ol class="tm-flow"><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1768729341334-666d6fe1385a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=400&q=75" alt="fresh turmeric roots with green leaves" width="400" height="400" loading="lazy"></figure><span>01</span><b>Harvest</b><p>Roots are dug up about nine months after planting.</p></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1570283988059-af8412f4fe91?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=400&q=75" alt="a marble mortar and pestle" width="400" height="400" loading="lazy"></figure><span>02</span><b>Boil, dry, grind</b><p>Roots are boiled, sun-dried until hard, then ground to a fine powder.</p></li><li class="rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1782061036200-79fee9a08a6d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=400&q=75" alt="ground spices in small bowls at a market" width="400" height="400" loading="lazy"></figure><span>03</span><b>To market</b><p>Sold whole, dried or ground, alongside its spice-box neighbours.</p></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="tm-s tm-ds"><div class="tm-w"><div class="tm-sh tm-sh-c"><p class="tm-ey"><svg class="tm-rt" viewBox="0 0 60 30" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 18c6-10 18-12 26-8s18 2 24-4c2 6-2 14-12 16s-16 0-22 2S6 26 4 18z"/><path d="M20 12c-2-4 0-8 4-10M38 12c2-4 6-6 10-6" /></svg> On the table</p><h2 class="rv">Three ways to use it tonight</h2></div><div class="tm-ds-g"><figure class="tm-dish rv"><div><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1767114915989-c6ab3c8fc42e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=460&h=460&q=75" alt="three bowls of curry with rice and spices" width="460" height="460" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption>Everyday curry</figcaption></figure><figure class="tm-dish rv"><div><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1782931608916-e47d6972a9de?auto=format&fit=crop&w=460&h=460&q=75" alt="yellow spiced rice in small red bowls" width="460" height="460" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption>Turmeric rice</figcaption></figure><figure class="tm-dish rv"><div><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1694849789325-914b71ab4075?auto=format&fit=crop&w=460&h=460&q=75" alt="a crisp dosa with sambar and chutneys" width="460" height="460" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption>Sambar &amp; dosa</figcaption></figure></div></div></section>

